  caps (5, 5, 2, 6, 2)  n=35,789
      E(L) = 0                       HOLDS
      |J| = 35   sum(|A_i|-1) = 35   HOLDS
      join/meet closed: 0 leaks, BUDGET 200,000 random pairs (seed 122) of 640,408,366  HOLDS
      rank(a v b)+rank(a ^ b)=rank(a)+rank(b): 0 failures  HOLDS
      cylinder factorises over the transfer: factor_q = 0  HOLDS

  NOTE on the fourth identity: rank is the coordinate sum (fixed in section 0 and confirmed
  against L2474 by 18 levels with 122 widest at rank 11).  Componentwise max + min = a + b
  in every coordinate, so rank(a v b) + rank(a ^ b) = rank(a) + rank(b) is ENTAILED by the
  third identity: wherever join and meet stay inside the lattice the fourth cannot fail.
  It is an exact identity, not an independent test, and the table prints the two in the
  same voice and with the same "tested by pairs" qualifier.

