4.  32.4 L9069-L9077 -- the recursion table, occupancy against cells and alphabets
================================================================================================
  0 - the index            cells 10  alphabets [4, 4]  box 16  printed 0.625  measured 0.625  EXACT
  1 - claims about it      cells 10  alphabets [10, 7]  box 70  printed 0.143  measured 0.143  EXACT
  2 - claims about those   cells 10  alphabets [10, 10]  box 100  printed 0.100  measured 0.100  EXACT
  3                        cells 10  alphabets [10, 10]  box 100  printed 0.100  measured 0.100  EXACT

  L9079 prints "Closure, dimension and E are invariant from level 1."
  measured from the table itself: closed = yes and E = 0 at levels 0,1,2,3; the number of
  alphabets (the dimension) is 2 at levels 0,1,2,3.  All three are invariant from level 0,
  not from level 1 -- the sentence understates its own table.  What changes at level 1 is
  occupancy (0.625 -> 0.143) and the alphabets ([4,4] -> [10,7]), which are exactly the two
  the same paragraph says stabilise "by level 2, not level 1".  CONSISTENT but understated.

