5.  32.4.1 L9100-L9108 -- the closure-operator proof, corroborated as the book corroborates it
================================================================================================
  CONVENTION: ambient box = the 8 coordinate value sets of L8_at((3,3,1,3,1)); a random
  subset is 3..40 cells drawn uniformly without replacement; 3,000 draws, seed 122;
  extensive/monotone/idempotent tested per draw exactly as the proof states them.
  extensive  failures 0 / 3,000        ZERO
  monotone   failures 0 / 3,000        ZERO
  idempotent failures 0 / 3,000        ZERO

  fixed points closed under intersection: 3,000 random pairs of fixed points, seed 122.
  non-empty meets 2,955 / 3,000 (98.5%)   book prints 2,873 / 3,000 (95.8%)
  closure failures on the meets: 0   ZERO, as printed
  NOTE the 2,873 is a draw-dependent count, not an invariant: it is reproducible only with
  the original seed and sampler.  Recorded as corroborated in kind, not matched exactly.

